# DISTRICT HEAD REGULATION
TASIKMALAYA DISTRICT
NUMBER 78 OF 2016

CONCERNING

SECOND AMENDMENT TO TASIKMALAYA DISTRICT HEAD REGULATION
NUMBER 37 OF 2014 CONCERNING POSITION, ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE,
DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS, AND WORK PROCEDURES
OF THE REGIONAL SECRETARIAT AND SECRETARIAT
OF THE REGIONAL PEOPLE'S REPRESENTATIVE COUNCIL

WITH THE BLESSING OF GOD ALMIGHTY

TASIKMALAYA DISTRICT HEAD,

Considering : a. that to implement the provisions of Article 4 paragraph (2) of Tasikmalaya District Regulation Number 8 of 2016 concerning Formation and Composition of Regional Apparatus, it is necessary to adjust the organizational structure, duties and functions, and work procedures of the Regional Secretariat and Secretariat of the Regional People's Representative Council;

b. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, it is necessary to stipulate a District Head Regulation concerning Second Amendment to Tasikmalaya District Head Regulation Number 37 of 2014 concerning Position, Organizational Structure, Duties and Functions, and Work Procedures of the Regional Secretariat and Secretariat of the Regional People's Representative Council;

In view of : 1. Law Number 14 of 1950 concerning Formation of Regions within West Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 8, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 9) as amended by Law Number 4 of 1968 concerning Formation of Tasikmalaya District and Tasikmalaya City by Separating Them from the Level II Tasikmalaya Region (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1968 Number 31, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2851);

2. Law Number 28 of 1999 concerning State Administration that is Clean and Free from Corruption, Collusion and Nepotism (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 75, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3851);

3. Law Number 17 of 2003 concerning State Finance (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 47, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4286);

4. Law Number 1 of 2004 concerning State Treasury (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 5, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4355);

5. Law Number 15 of 2004 concerning Audit of Management and Responsibility of State Finance (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 66, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4400);

6. Law Number 33 of 2004 concerning Financial Balance between Central Government and Regional Governments (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 126, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4438);

7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

8. Government Regulation Number 58 of 2005 concerning Regional Financial Management (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 140, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4578);

9. Government Regulation Number 79 of 2005 concerning Guidelines for Guidance and Supervision of Regional Government Administration (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2005 Number 165, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4593);

10. Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning Division of Government Affairs between the Government, Provincial Regional Governments, and District/City Regional Governments (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 82, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4737);

11. Government Regulation Number 41 of 2007 concerning Regional Apparatus Organization (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 89, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4741);

12. Government Regulation Number 18 of 2016 concerning Regional Apparatus (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 114, Supplement to State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5887);

13. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 57 of 2007 concerning Technical Guidelines for Organizational Structuring of Regions;

14. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 13 of 2006 concerning Guidelines for Regional Financial Management as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 59 of 2007 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 13 of 2006 concerning Guidelines for Regional Financial Management (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 50);

15. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning Formation of Regional Legal Products (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 2036);

16. Tasikmalaya District Regulation Number 4 of 2008 concerning Principles of Regional Financial Management (Tasikmalaya District Gazette of 2008 Number 4 Series E) as amended by Tasikmalaya District Regulation Number 2 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Tasikmalaya District Regulation Number 4 of 2008 concerning Principles of Regional Financial Management (Tasikmalaya District Gazette of 2014 Number 2 Series E);

17. Tasikmalaya District Regulation Number 8 of 2016 concerning Formation and Composition of Regional Apparatus (Tasikmalaya District Gazette of 2016 Number 8);

HAS DECIDED:

To stipulate : DISTRICT HEAD REGULATION CONCERNING SECOND AMENDMENT TO TASIKMALAYA DISTRICT HEAD REGULATION NUMBER 37 OF 2014 CONCERNING POSITION, ORGANIZATIONAL STRUCTURE, DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS, AND WORK PROCEDURES OF THE REGIONAL SECRETARIAT AND SECRETARIAT OF THE REGIONAL PEOPLE'S REPRESENTATIVE COUNCIL.

Article I

Several provisions in Tasikmalaya District Head Regulation Number 37 of 2014 concerning Position, Organizational Structure, Duties and Functions, and Work Procedures of the Regional Secretariat and Secretariat of the Regional People's Representative Council (Tasikmalaya District Gazette of 2014 Number 37) as amended by Tasikmalaya District Head Regulation Number 64 of 2015 concerning Amendment to Tasikmalaya District Head Regulation Number 37 of 2014 concerning Position, Organizational Structure, Duties and Functions, and Work Procedures of the Regional Secretariat and Secretariat of the Regional People's Representative Council (Tasikmalaya District Gazette of 2015 Number 64) are amended as follows:

1. The provisions of Article 2 are amended so that Article 2 reads as follows:

Article 2

(1) Regional Secretariat has the duty to assist the District Head in carrying out government affairs which are the authority of the Region and administrative tasks.

(2) Regional Secretariat in carrying out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1) performs the following functions:
a. coordination of preparation of regional policies;
b. coordination of implementation of duties of Regional Apparatus;
c. monitoring and evaluation of implementation of regional policies;
d. administrative services;
e. fostering of Regional Secretariat apparatus; and
f. implementation of other duties assigned by the District Head in accordance with their duties and functions.

2. The provisions of Article 3 are amended so that Article 3 reads as follows:

Article 3

(1) Regional Secretariat consists of:
a. Secretariat;
b. General Section;
c. Government Section;
d. Welfare Section;
e. Economy and Development Section; and
f. Functional Group.

(2) General Section as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b consists of:
a. Legal Sub-Section;
b. Organization Sub-Section; and
c. Public Relations and Protocol Sub-Section.

(3) Government Section as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c consists of:
a. Administration Sub-Section; and
b. Territorial Government Sub-Section.

(4) Welfare Section as referred to in paragraph (1) letter d consists of:
a. People's Welfare Sub-Section; and
b. Social Assistance Sub-Section.

(5) Economy and Development Section as referred to in paragraph (1) letter e consists of:
a. Economy Sub-Section; and
b. Development Administration Sub-Section.

3. The provisions of Article 4 are amended so that Article 4 reads as follows:

Article 4

(1) Secretariat as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (1) letter a has the duty to carry out coordination of preparation of regional policies, coordination of implementation of duties of Regional Apparatus, monitoring and evaluation of implementation of regional policies, administrative services, and fostering of Regional Secretariat apparatus.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), Secretariat performs the following functions:
a. coordination of preparation of regional policies;
b. coordination of implementation of duties of Regional Apparatus;
c. monitoring and evaluation of implementation of regional policies;
d. coordination of administrative services;
e. coordination of fostering of Regional Secretariat apparatus; and
f. implementation of other duties assigned by the Regional Secretary in accordance with their duties and functions.

4. The provisions of Article 5 are amended so that Article 5 reads as follows:

Article 5

(1) General Section as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (1) letter b has the duty to carry out coordination of legal affairs, organization, public relations and protocol, and general affairs.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), General Section performs the following functions:
a. coordination of legal affairs;
b. coordination of organizational affairs;
c. coordination of public relations and protocol affairs;
d. coordination of general affairs; and
e. implementation of other duties assigned by the Regional Secretary in accordance with their duties and functions.

5. The provisions of Article 6 are amended so that Article 6 reads as follows:

Article 6

(1) Legal Sub-Section as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (2) letter a has the duty to carry out legal affairs.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), Legal Sub-Section performs the following functions:
a. preparation of materials for legal policy formulation;
b. preparation of materials for legal counseling;
c. preparation of materials for legal advocacy;
d. preparation of materials for legal documentation;
e. preparation of materials for legal consultation;
f. preparation of materials for legal opinion;
g. preparation of materials for review of draft regional regulations and draft district head regulations;
h. preparation of materials for review of cooperation agreements;
i. preparation of materials for legal consideration; and
j. implementation of other duties assigned by the Head of General Section in accordance with their duties and functions.

6. The provisions of Article 7 are amended so that Article 7 reads as follows:

Article 7

(1) Organization Sub-Section as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (2) letter b has the duty to carry out organizational affairs.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), Organization Sub-Section performs the following functions:
a. preparation of materials for organizational policy formulation;
