g. preparation of materials for coordination of culture affairs; and
h. implementation of other duties assigned by the Head of Welfare Section in accordance with their duties and functions.

14. The provisions of Article 14 are amended so that Article 14 reads as follows:

Article 14

(1) Social Assistance Sub-Section as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (4) letter b has the duty to carry out social assistance affairs.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), Social Assistance Sub-Section performs the following functions:
a. preparation of materials for social assistance policy formulation;
b. preparation of materials for coordination of social assistance to political parties;
c. preparation of materials for coordination of social assistance to community organizations;
d. preparation of materials for coordination of social assistance to religious organizations;
e. preparation of materials for coordination of social assistance to educational institutions;
f. preparation of materials for coordination of social assistance to other institutions; and
g. implementation of other duties assigned by the Head of Welfare Section in accordance with their duties and functions.

15. The provisions of Article 15 are amended so that Article 15 reads as follows:

Article 15

(1) Economy and Development Section as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (1) letter e has the duty to carry out coordination of economy affairs and development administration.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), Economy and Development Section performs the following functions:
a. coordination of economy affairs;
b. coordination of development administration affairs; and
c. implementation of other duties assigned by the Regional Secretary in accordance with their duties and functions.

16. The provisions of Article 16 are amended so that Article 16 reads as follows:

Article 16

(1) Economy Sub-Section as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (5) letter a has the duty to carry out economy affairs.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), Economy Sub-Section performs the following functions:
a. preparation of materials for economy policy formulation;
b. preparation of materials for coordination of agriculture affairs;
c. preparation of materials for coordination of trade affairs;
d. preparation of materials for coordination of industry affairs;
e. preparation of materials for coordination of cooperatives and small and medium enterprises affairs;
f. preparation of materials for coordination of investment affairs;
g. preparation of materials for coordination of tourism affairs; and
h. implementation of other duties assigned by the Head of Economy and Development Section in accordance with their duties and functions.

17. The provisions of Article 17 are amended so that Article 17 reads as follows:

Article 17

(1) Development Administration Sub-Section as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (5) letter b has the duty to carry out development administration affairs.

(2) To carry out the duties as referred to in paragraph (1), Development Administration Sub-Section performs the following functions:
a. preparation of materials for development administration policy formulation;
b. preparation of materials for coordination of public works affairs;
c. preparation of materials for coordination of spatial planning affairs;
d. preparation of materials for coordination of housing affairs;
e. preparation of materials for coordination of environment affairs;
f. preparation of materials for coordination of transportation affairs;
g. preparation of materials for coordination of communication and information affairs; and
h. implementation of other duties assigned by the Head of Economy and Development Section in accordance with their duties and functions.

18. The provisions of Article 18 are amended so that Article 18 reads as follows:

Article 18

Functional Group as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (1) letter f has the duty to carry out functional activities in accordance with their expertise and skills.

Article II

This District Head Regulation comes into force on the date of promulgation.

In order that everyone may know of it, the promulgation of this District Head Regulation is ordered by placing it in the Tasikmalaya District Gazette.

